matrisaver for Debian / Ubuntu
==============================

Running it
----------

    matrisaver --run            fullscreen on every monitor
    matrisaver --window         a single window, for a look
    matrisaver --list-monitors  what the compositor reports
    matrisaver --list-adapters  what wgpu can see
    man matrisaver              every flag, and the exit codes

Idle integration
----------------

MatriSaver does not watch for idleness. Every desktop already ships an
idle daemon, and a competing one is how a screensaver ends up
interrupting a presentation. Point your session's daemon at MatriSaver
instead.

GNOME and KDE manage idle and screen blanking themselves; use their own
settings, or run MatriSaver from a keyboard shortcut.

For sway, Hyprland, river and other Wayland sessions, and for plain X11
sessions, a wrapper that picks the right daemon ships at
/usr/libexec/matrisaver/matrisaver-idle, driven by a systemd **user**
unit:

    systemctl --user enable --now matrisaver-idle.service

It must be a user unit. A system unit has no WAYLAND_DISPLAY or DISPLAY,
so MatriSaver would exit 4 (no display session) every time. If the unit
starts before your compositor has published its environment, add this to
the compositor's autostart:

    systemctl --user import-environment WAYLAND_DISPLAY DISPLAY XDG_RUNTIME_DIR

Worked examples for each daemon are in
/usr/share/matrisaver/integration.

Not a screen locker
-------------------

MatriSaver draws; it does not authenticate, and it does not block input
beyond its own window. Any key or mouse click dismisses it. Keep your
desktop's own lock in charge of locking and chain it after the
screensaver if you want both — do not substitute one for the other.

GPU backends
------------

Vulkan is tried first, then GL. The chosen rung is reported on stderr:

    SURFACE host=linux rung=vulkan backend=Vulkan adapter=... device_type=...

Each demotion prints a FALLBACK line with a reason, and a total failure
exits 3 with the list of what was tried. Install mesa-vulkan-drivers for
the Vulkan path or libgl1-mesa-dri for the GL path; the package
Recommends both so either is usually present.

Overlays
--------

The ASCII silhouette overlay reads images from, in precedence order:

    $MATRISAVER_OVERLAY_DIR
    $XDG_DATA_HOME/matrisaver/overlays   (default ~/.local/share/...)
    /usr/local/share/matrisaver/overlays
    /usr/share/matrisaver/overlays       (shipped by this package)

Drop high-contrast portraits or logos into the per-user directory to
have them woven into the cycle; they take precedence over the shipped
pack, so nothing needs root.
